    "rationale": "NiryatAI proposal: # HS Code for Cotton T-Shirts\n\nGreat question! Let me break this down clearly.\n\n## The HS Code\n\n**For cotton t-shirts, the relevant HS code is:**\n- **6109** (HS Chapter 61 \u2014 Knitted or crocheted apparel)\n- More specifically: **61091000** (T-shirts of cotton, knitted)\n\nSome variants you might encounter:\n- **6109.10.00** \u2014 T-shirts of cotton (knitted)\n- **6109.90.00** \u2014 T-shirts of other materials (if not pure cotton)\n\n---\n\n## Exporting to Germany \u2014 Key Points\n\n**Good news:** The HS code itself **remains the same regardless of destination**. However, what *changes* is the **duty treatment**:\n\n### 1. **Germany is in the EU**\n   - As an EU member, Germany follows the **Common External Tariff (CET)**\n   - Duty rates are set at the EU level, not individually by Germany\n\n### 2. **You Need to Check:**\n   - **EU Import Duty Rate** for HS code 6109 (typically **12% for cotton t-shirts**, but verify current rates)\n   - **Preferential rates** if you qualify under trade agreements (e.g., GSP \u2014 Generalised System of Preferences for India)\n\n### 3. **How to Verify**\n   - Check the **TARIC database** (EU's integrated tariff system): [ec.europa.eu/taxation_customs/taric](https://ec.europa.eu/taxation_customs/taric)\n   - Or check the **Indian Trade Portal** for duty rates to EU countries\n\n---\n\n## For Your Export Pricing\n\n**Use this formula:**\n- **CIF Price (Cost + Insurance + Freight) \u00d7 (1 + Duty %) = Landed Cost**\n- This helps you quote competitively to German buyers\n\n---\n\nWould you like help with:\n- **Finding German buyers** for cotton t-shirts?\n- **Calculating FOB/CIF pricing** for this product?\n- **Registration/export documentation** steps?\n\nLet me know! \ud83d\ude80\nTradeStat commodity: T-SHIRTS ETC OF COTTON\nMarket signal: Hard to enter \u2014 India barely present",
